**This plugin** (author: replace this line): what it does, where its logic
lives, and what to read before a change (this file, `DESIGN.md`, the module).

This directory is one N.E.K.O plugin: its own Git repository and its editable
source. `plugin.toml` holds the identity (`[plugin].id`, `[plugin].entry`; never
rename them). The plugin already exists: do not run `neko-plugin init` again.
Deeper guides: `.agents/skills/neko-plugin/` (start at `SKILL.md`). They call
this directory `<plugin_dir>`; inside a N.E.K.O checkout it lives at
`plugin/plugins/<plugin_id>/`.

## Route

- **A, source checkout (recommended for plugin development)**: a N.E.K.O
  checkout (a folder whose `pyproject.toml` says `name = "N.E.K.O"`) is
  reachable: the Verify commands below already point at it, or this plugin
  sits inside it. Check with the `check` command below (or
  `uv run neko-plugin --help` in the checkout). Every check runs here.
- **B, desktop build (fallback)**: no checkout (the Verify commands still show
  `<path-to-this-directory>` and no checkout exists). The desktop app is for
  using N.E.K.O; developing here works, but verification is limited: no
  `neko-plugin` command runs (check, lint, sync, precheck, build), so say so
  instead of guessing. App buttons still work (they are not the CLI):
  Start/Reload on the plugin page, its Logs tab, and Build package in the
  Plugin studio (插件制作工作台).
- **Moving to A**: when Route B blocks a check, ask the user whether to set up
  a N.E.K.O source checkout, and change nothing until they agree. It needs
  git and uv (plus Node.js to run N.E.K.O from source), and the desktop app
  must be fully quit before the source version starts. Steps: "Setting Up
  Route A" in `.agents/skills/neko-plugin/references/plugin-cli-and-debugging.md`.

## Hard Constraints

Full reasons: `.agents/skills/neko-plugin/references/execution-boundary.md`.

1. **Do not edit N.E.K.O itself**: host changes never reach users of this plugin.
2. **Do not import host internals** (`utils.*`, `plugin.core`, `plugin.sdk.shared`, ...): they bypass consent disclosure and break without notice; use `plugin.sdk.plugin` (adapters: `plugin.sdk.adapter`).
3. **Do not call N.E.K.O's local services directly**: ports differ per install and it bypasses permission checks; use the SDK.
4. **Do not use `print`**: it never reaches the plugin log; use `self.logger`.
5. **Do not log conversation text, secrets, or tokens**: logs are shared files; log lengths, IDs, error types.
6. **Do not hard-code paths**: write with `self.data_path()` / `self.cache_path()`; `self.plugin_dir` is read-only.
7. **Do not block the event loop**: all entries share one loop; use async libraries or `await asyncio.to_thread(...)`.
8. **Do not use `requirements.txt`**: the host reads `pyproject.toml` `[project].dependencies`, loaded only from `vendor/`.
9. **Do not commit `vendor/`, binaries, or files over 2 MiB**: `sync` regenerates `vendor/`; the Market rejects binaries and oversized source files.
10. **Do not use `eval`/`exec`/`pickle`/`shell=True`/`verify=False`**: they run untrusted code or disable TLS checks.

## Code Essentials

- Reuse before adding; merge logic once it appears a third time; a
  replacement deletes the old code (no `_v2`/`_old` copies or switches).
- A new dependency needs a stated reason, an exact `==` pin, and preferably a
  release at least 7 days old. Stop and ask before going well past the request.
- Entries: `@plugin_entry` on `async def`, return `Ok(data)` or `Err(SdkError("..."))`
  (`Err` reaches the caller as a failed call). Validated input:
  `params=Model` (Pydantic). `llm_result_fields=[...]` picks what the
  AI reads. A Pydantic return annotation (`-> Model`) is the output contract,
  checked at runtime (warning by default, failure with `strict_output=True`);
  an explicit `output_schema=` mapping is published, not checked.
- The host injects `_ctx` (run id, character name, timeout); declare a
  `_ctx` parameter only if you need it.
- User-visible text (names, descriptions, UI) goes through `[plugin.i18n]`
  locale files with at least `zh-CN` and `en`.
- Await `self.config`/`plugins`/`store`/`db` calls, `finish`, and
  `ctx.models`/`ctx.images`. Never await `push_message`: it has already queued
  the message and then raises `TypeError`, so a retry sends it twice.
- `self.config` raises on failure; `plugins`/`store`/`db` return `Ok`/`Err`,
  which are always truthy: test `.is_ok()`. `self.store` stores nothing unless
  `[plugin.store] enabled = true`, yet `set` still returns `Ok`.
- `push_message` targets a character only via `target_lanlan=`: keep
  `_ctx["lanlan_name"]` from the entry (timers and threads have no `_ctx`).
- Hook decorators (`before_entry`, `hook`, ...) never run today; `@message`
  handlers get no host messages (only another plugin's `call_event`).
- Routers: list them in `__routers__` and `include_router` them in `__init__`;
  `@ui.context` works only on the main class. Hosted TSX: write
  `props.api.call(...)`, and use `useConfirm()`, not a `confirm` prop.
- Market: id matches `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$` (at most 100 characters); the
  release tag is `v<version>`; the GitHub repo is conventionally
  `n.e.k.o_plugin_<id>`. `type = "extension"` was removed
  ([migration guide](https://github.com/Project-N-E-K-O/N.E.K.O/blob/main/docs/plugins/migration-v0.9.md));
  use `type = "plugin"`.

## Runtime Model

Details: `.agents/skills/neko-plugin/references/runtime-model.md`.

- One process per plugin. `startup`, the entry loop, each timer tick, and
  `shutdown` run in **separate** event loops.
- `startup` must return fast (timeout 10 s by default). Tasks it creates are
  cancelled when it returns; clients/locks it creates belong to a dead loop.
- Periodic work: `@timer_interval(id=..., seconds=...)`, run in its own thread
  with a fresh loop per tick.
- Entries time out after 10 s by default (raise `timeout=` for LLM calls);
  calls to other plugins are capped at 60 s, with no cycle detection
  (`self.ctx.call_chain` shows who called you, only inside an entry call;
  it is empty in timers and bare threads).
- Reload starts a new process (memory is lost; persist with `data_path`). A
  crashed plugin is not restarted automatically.

## Verify

{command_context}

```bash
{check_command}
{lint_command}
{sync_command}
{precheck_command}
```

While iterating, run `check`; `check -r` adds `tests/` and a package build.
Before reporting done, run the four lines in order; `precheck` is the Market CI
gate (lint, `sync --clean`, `check -r`). Outside the checkout's built-in plugin
folder, `check -r` and `precheck` stop on uncommitted changes before any test
runs, so they pass only after a commit; inside it they skip Git checks.
Commit only in this plugin's own repository, never in an enclosing N.E.K.O
checkout, and never unasked; otherwise report what is still unverified.
Ruff is pinned and runs with `--ignore-noqa`, so `# noqa` does not silence it:
fix the code.
Build a package with `{build_command}`.
Route B: none of these `neko-plugin` commands run. If `README.md` shows a
pinned `uvx ruff==...` line, run it: that lint needs only `uv` (its version
is fixed when the project is generated and can trail Market CI). Review the
code against the constraints above, then ask the user to Start/Reload and
report back; packages come from Build package in the Plugin studio.

## When Something Fails

| Symptom | Cause | Do |
|---|---|---|
| `MissingPythonDependencies` | dependency declared but not in `vendor/` | run `sync --clean`, then reload. Route B: tell the user; remove the dependency or switch to Route A |
| `ImportError` on a third-party package | not declared, or not synced | add it to `pyproject.toml`, `sync --clean` |
| `ImportError` on `utils`/`plugin.sdk.shared`/... | host internal | use the public SDK (constraint 2) |
| `neko-plugin`: command not found / unknown command | not in a checkout, or an old CLI | run `uv run neko-plugin --help` from the N.E.K.O root; Route B: no CLI |
| No N.E.K.O checkout | Route B | say what cannot be verified; do not invent results |
| startup failed or timed out | exception or slow `startup` | read the plugin log; keep `startup` short |
| `Entry must be 'async def'` | sync handler | make it `async def` |
| `Plugin event-loop stall` | blocking call in a handler | async library or `asyncio.to_thread` |

When the user is not a developer: say what cannot be done, why, and what they
can choose instead. Do not ask them whether N.E.K.O should be changed.

